sequenceDiagram
    actor User as CLI User
    participant SC as SetupCommand + SetupWalkthrough
    participant FS as Local Filesystem
    participant AWS as SetupAws (STS, IAM, S3, DynamoDB)
    participant CF as AWS CloudFormation
    participant IB as Image Builder

    Note over User,IB: baas admin deployment setup -- eleven steps, each checks reality first.<br/>On a terminal it asks and waits for Enter at a step the user must do outside baas.<br/>Unattended (--non-interactive, a redirect, CI) it exits 1 there. Nothing records progress.
    User->>SC: baas [--deployment D] admin deployment setup [--region] [--deployer-aws-profile]<br/>[--policy-file F] [--github-org --github-repo | --revoke-github-oidc] [--build-image] [--non-interactive]
    Note over SC: a partial federation set is a usage error, before anything is loaded

    SC->>FS: 1. which deployment -- local files only, no AWS call
    alt two or more configured and no D
        SC-->>User: interactive - choose one, or a new one. Unattended - refused, exit 2
    end
    SC->>AWS: 2. GetCallerIdentity with the deployer profile (stored one is the default)
    alt credentials unusable or SSO expired
        SC-->>User: aws configure / aws sso login -- wait, or exit 1
    end
    Note over SC: 3. new deployment - name (baas-ACCOUNT suggested, any valid name) and region.<br/>Existing - both shown, never asked
    SC->>AWS: BucketProbe -- a reachable bucket in another region means the deployment lives there
    alt deployment lives in another region
        SC-->>User: setup --region THERE, exit 1, no delete advice
    end

    SC->>AWS: 4. render the deployer policy, SimulatePrincipalPolicy (15 calls, Enter only)
    alt denied
        SC-->>User: saved to policy.json or printed (unattended - stdout), and the IAM admin's commands
        User->>SC: Enter once attached -- check again
    else not checked
        Note over SC: shown as not checked, never met -- the run continues
    end

    SC->>CF: 5. stack status -- for a create (absent or ROLLBACK_COMPLETE) check the names
    SC->>AWS: BucketProbe and DescribeTable
    alt bucket held by another account
        SC-->>User: interactive - back to 3 for another name (then 4 again). Unattended - exit 1
    else leftover bucket or table here
        SC-->>User: name it and its removal command, delete nothing -- wait, or exit 1
    end
    opt the stack is present
        SC->>CF: DescribeStacks - the BaasCliVersion it records
        alt this CLI is an older release
            SC-->>User: both versions and the installer's curl line -- exit 1, never a wait
        else an unreleased build
            SC-->>User: not checked (stderr)
        end
    end

    Note over SC: 6. GitHub Actions - asked on a terminal, or from the options.<br/>Unchanged federation is carried forward
    opt federation trusted
        SC->>AWS: GetOpenIDConnectProvider(token.actions.githubusercontent.com in this account)
        alt present without the sts.amazonaws.com audience
            SC-->>User: never modified - the admin's add-client-id command -- wait, or exit 1
        end
    end

    opt 7. interactive, and creating or an answer changed
        SC-->>User: the plan - account, region, name, create or update, GitHub, about $0.20 a month
        User->>SC: confirm (a no, or a closed input, changes nothing - exit 1)
    end

    SC->>CF: 8. wait while the stack is *_IN_PROGRESS (an interrupted run)
    opt provider absent
        SC->>AWS: CreateOpenIDConnectProvider (Url, ClientIDList only)
    end
    alt create
        SC->>CF: CreateStack (explicit federation, every image parameter, BaasCliVersion if released)
        SC->>FS: write deployments/D.yaml as soon as the create is accepted (region, profile if proven)
        SC->>CF: wait for CREATE_COMPLETE
    else update
        SC->>CF: UpdateStack (changed params and a released BaasCliVersion, UsePreviousValue for every other declared one)
        opt BaasCliVersion raised
            SC-->>User: CLIs older than this release now refuse the deployment (stderr, nothing asked)
        end
    end
    alt a permission failure
        SC-->>User: the policy and the admin's commands -- Enter returns to 4. Unattended - exit 1
    end

    SC->>AWS: 9. AssumeRole into D-role-operator, retried ~30 s for IAM propagation
    SC->>IB: 10. image - running build? current image?
    alt a build is running
        SC->>IB: wait for it and publish it (asked first on a terminal)
    else absent or older base
        SC->>IB: offered (default yes), unattended only with --build-image - build or adopt, publish
    end

    SC->>FS: 11. deployments/D.yaml - the deployer profile only on evidence it can deploy
    SC-->>User: next steps, each with --deployment D - first run, a teammate's grant and config sync,<br/>gh variable set lines, and on a changing interactive run the repeat command
    SC-->>User: exit 0
